<title>ITALY: Visco sees no lasting impact from Italy VAT change.</title>
<headline>Visco sees no lasting impact from Italy VAT change.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance Minister Vincenzo Visco said on Thursday that any changes to certain VAT rates in Italy as a result of European Union harmonisation requirements would not have a lasting impact on inflation.</p>
<p>&quot;This operation could have an impact, a little rise, but the effect on prices will not be lasting,&quot; he told a budget commission meeting of the Senate (upper house) on the government's 1998-2000 economic forecasts.</p>
<p>--Rome newsroom +39 6 678 2505</p>
</text>
